{"s":[[null,1,[["t",[[[["l","小桶生产力","No Profession"]],[["l","小桶生产力 - 农耕人","Tiller"]],[["l","小桶生产力 - 工匠","Artisan"]]]]],["p",["This page lists the productivity of processing ",["l","水果","Fruits"],", ",["l","蔬菜","Vegetables"],", ",["l","咖啡豆","Coffee Bean"],"s, and ",["l","蜂蜜","Honey"]," into ",["l","工匠物品","Artisan Goods"]," in a ",["l","小桶","Keg"],"."]],["p",["The products produced usually sell for more than the raw input items, so using a Keg is almost always profitable. Items that lose gold are highlighted in red, and items whose net increase in value is zero are highlighted in orange. The profit made from processing items is lowest when using iridium quality and highest when using regular quality items. ",["l","啤酒","Beer"],", ",["l","蜜蜂酒","Mead"],", ",["l","淡啤酒","Pale Ale"],", and ",["l","果酒","Wine"]," can be aged in a ",["l","木桶","Cask"]," to further increase their profit. The table below shows profit for regular quality processed items only."]],["p",["This table does not take into account the effects of Tiller or Artisan ",["l","耕种","professions"],", which reduce and increase the profit from a ",["l","小桶","Keg"],", respectively. To view the profitability for those professions, use the links at the top of the page."]],["p",["Note that the processing times for a Keg vary, depending on the item used."]],["l",0,[[1,[["l","啤酒","Beer"]," = 1,750 minutes"]],[1,[["l","咖啡","Coffee"]," = 120 minutes"]],[1,[["l","绿茶","Green Tea"]," = 180 minutes"]],[1,[["l","果汁","Juice"]," = 6,000 minutes"]],[1,[["l","蜜蜂酒","Mead"]," = 600 minutes"]],[1,[["l","淡啤酒","Pale Ale"]," = 2,250 minutes"]],[1,[["l","醋","Vinegar"]," = 600 minutes"]],[1,[["l","果酒","Wine"]," = 10,000 minutes"]]]],["p",["For items that take less than a day to process (e.g., Coffee), the table calculates maximum profit assuming the player continually harvests and refills the keg during a 1600 minute day. [1]"]],["p",["Productivity (g/minute) = ([Processed Sell Price] - [Input Item Sell Price]) / Processing Time"]],["p",["